<h2>Who this is for</h2>
<p>Anyone with an X-300 (or thinking of reusing one) who wants it to do more than its built-in thermostat mode: night setbacks, office hours, short-cycle protection, or reacting to a value pushed in from another device. You don't need to have programmed before; the tutorials start from nothing.</p>

<div class="warn"><p><strong>This is an unofficial simulator.</strong> It follows the BASIC rules in the X-300 users manual and what real units were seen doing, but it is not ControlByWeb's interpreter. Always run the vendor's own syntax checker, keep a copy of the script that's on the unit now, and watch the unit after you upload. <a href="/about/">What is and isn't known</a>.</p></div>
